{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.MarkovTraceOnHecke","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Hom"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.MarkovStabilization.stabilizes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.MarkovStabilization.stabilizes","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Markov stabilization: `tr_{n+1}(ι x) = tr_n x` for every `x` at level `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.MarkovStabilization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.MarkovStabilization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.MarkovStabilization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.MarkovStabilization","kind":"class","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L82-L102","doc":"**§3b DEPENDENT conjecture — Markov trace stabilization (bean `qou-ep0a`).**\nGIVEN two Hecke braided presentations (levels `n` and `n+1`, threaded as the two\n`[HeckeBraidedPresentation …]` binders — these binders ARE the dependency edge,\nmaking this conjecture *conditional on* the primary) together with the tower\ninclusion `ι : Hn →ₐ Hn1`, the Markov traces are **compatible with the inclusion**:\n`tr_{n+1}(ι x) = tr_n x`.\n\nThis stabilization is exactly what promotes the per-level trace (`H3.trM`,\nproved) to a general-`n` Markov trace, and it is the input the derived\n`observationFrame` needs to be tower-stable. Content-bearing (a real quantified\nequation). Base cases n=2,3 are the concrete Markov reductions\n(`QOU.Machinery.H3.trM_markov_σ₁`); general `n` is OPEN — **no instance**.\nDEPENDENT: it binds `HeckeBraidedPresentation`, so the dependency is visible in\nthe type (never smuggled as an unconditional assertion). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.heckeQuadratic_h2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.heckeQuadratic_h2","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L62-L78","doc":"**Concrete n=2 slice (non-vacuous, PROVED).** The 2-dimensional Hecke generator\nwith eigenvalues `q, −q⁻¹` (diagonal) satisfies the Hecke quadratic\n`σ² = (q − q⁻¹)·σ + 1`. Realizes the `hecke_quadratic` field content at n=2 (the\nsingle-generator case), complementing the n=3 operator identity\n`QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀_hecke`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.far_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.far_commute","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Far commutation `σᵢ σⱼ = σⱼ σᵢ` for `|i − j| ≥ 2` (monoidal interchange F1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.braid_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.braid_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Braid relation `σᵢ σᵢ₊₁ σᵢ = σᵢ₊₁ σᵢ σᵢ₊₁` — the Yang–Baxter / hexagon\nshadow (the braiding datum F2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Hecke quadratic relation `σᵢ² = (q − q⁻¹)·σᵢ + 1` (Skein / R-matrix\neigenvalue equation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeBraidedCategory.HeckeBraidedPresentation","kind":"class","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeBraidedCategoryScaffold.lean#L38-L60","doc":"**§3b PRIMARY conjecture — general-n Hecke braided presentation.**\nThe braid generators `σ : ℕ → H` of the inductive-limit Hecke algebra `H_∞(q)`\nsatisfy three relations: the Hecke quadratic (the R-matrix eigenvalue / Skein\nequation), the braid relation (the Yang–Baxter / braiding-hexagon shadow — the\nF2 datum), and far commutation (the monoidal-interchange F1 shadow). Over a field\n`R` (needs `q⁻¹`).\n\nContent-bearing (three real quantified equations, no `True`, no empty body).\nThis is the algebraic presentation of the braided monoidal SOURCE category `𝐂`\nthat τ's domain requires. **No instance for general n** — Mathlib has no `H_n(q)`\nfor n≥3, so this is the OPEN source-category infrastructure (F1/F2). PRIMARY: its\nsignature binds no other conjecture class. Concrete slices are proved at n=2\n(`heckeQuadratic_h2` below) and n=3 (`QOU.Machinery.H3.mulσ₀_hecke`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}